```java
// File: Main.java   (name matches the public class, capital M).
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {     // the entry point the launcher looks for.
        String who = args.length > 0 ? args[0] : "world";
        System.out.println("Hello, " + who + "!");
    }
}
```

```bash
javac Main.java          # creates Main.class.
java Main                # Hello, world!
java Main Asha           # Hello, Asha!
```

| Piece | Must be |
|---|---|
| file name. | same as the public class: Main.java. |
| class. | `public class Main`. |
| entry point. | `public static void main(String[] args)`. |
| launch. | `java Main` (class name). |

```reveal
{"prompt": "What if main is written as `static void main(String args)`?", "answer": "The classic launcher won't treat it as the entry point (wrong parameter type), so it reports that no suitable main method was found. The signature must match."}
```

